WEBVTT

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:02.890
99th Seisho Festival

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:02.890
Performance Day

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:09.750
Let's go! Together, we will grasp that star...

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:17.290
Though I release my arrow over and over,
it will not reach that star...

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:22.330
You, who so naively aim for that star...
how could you understand this fury?!

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.540
Me, I... I was sure I could grasp that star!

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.620
At least, that's what I thought.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:31.450
But that was nothing more than arrogance!

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:35.370
If you don't have the strength to face something,
you should just run away!

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:40.580
Yes. Running away was... it was all I could do!

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:44.330
And yet, in the midst of such lamentation and regret,

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:46.870
I remained spellbound!

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:50.700
This is envy... such terrible envy.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.830
If that's what you think, then tell me!

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.830
What must I give up to have that person for myself?

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:58.830
Ah, it repeats itself again.

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:03.870
The cycle of despair... That which lies below the starlight.

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:09.250
Our dream will not come to be.

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:19.120
Wow...

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:26.340
99th
Seisho Festival

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.200
It's so bright...

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:27.840
99th Seisho Festival

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:27.840
2 days after closing

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.100
Year 1 Group A & B

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.100
Joint Celebration Party

00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:36.230
99th Seisho Festival

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:43.200
This was the first performance of the 99th class
at the 99th Seisho Festival, "Starlight"!

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:46.120
The show was a huge success, and so we say...

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:47.290
Cheers!

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:48.620
Cheers!

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:07.500
Junna-chan, thanks for your hard work!

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:09.120
Nana...

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:11.290
We've only finished the first show, though.

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:14.040
We'll have to start preparing for next year soon.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:15.750
You're being hasty, though!

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:23.620
It was a huge success, huh, Karen-chan?

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.330
And you did good too, Nana!

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.250
Mahiru-chan, weren't you nervous?

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:32.830
Yes! But thanks to Karen-chan,
my heart stopped pounding.

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:36.450
It's the two leads.

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:38.040
That was an excellent performance!

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:40.330
Thank you very much.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.080
I am not losing to you.

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:47.580
Well then, let's audition again next year. Together.

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:51.950
Nana Daiba...

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:53.950
You too.

00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:55.080
Huh?

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:57.790
Maya...chan?

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:06.250
I thought I wouldn't get that goddess role,
but I managed it somehow!

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:09.790
I don't think "somehow" has anything
to do with it, do you?

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:13.250
Nana!

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:14.830
Futaba-chan?!

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:17.540
Thanks for helping out with so much!

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:20.950
Nana, you helped me quite a bit too.

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:23.870
You're really good at shoulder massages!

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:26.830
Me too! You came to practice with me!

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:29.620
And you were a big help with the costumes, too!

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:31.870
And with the background sets, too!

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:38.120
And when everyone was starving,
you made snacks for us...

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:43.910
I feel like it's thanks to the banana muffins you made
that we made it through the final stretch!

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:45.620
That's right!

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:46.620
Banana!

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:47.450
Huh?

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:50.660
Nana... You're like everyone's "banana," right?

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:53.290
You're sweet and kind and nourishing!

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:55.540
You can even ease stiff shoulders!

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.790
Nana is... a banana?

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:00.790
Oh, that's cute!

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:05.700
Even your height is... banana-like?

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:07.660
And you smell good, too!

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:12.500
A banana, huh?

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:19.160
Nana?!

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:21.750
D-did I say something wrong?!

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:23.040
Nana?

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:27.910
No... No, that's not it.

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:29.790
I'm happy!

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:31.620
I...

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:34.910
I'm so glad I came to this academy.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:41.450
I can't believe making a performance could be
so enjoyable, that it would shine so much.

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:46.160
This performance, the "Starlight"
of the 99th Seisho Festival...

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:47.450
I'll never forget it!

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:52.830
I've found best friends forever,
and the stage I was meant for.

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:56.500
She was born on this day...

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:59.330
The Stage Girl, Nana Daiba.

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:12.320
Revue Starlight

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:21.120
Ano hoshi o tsukamu no wa daare?
Who, oh who, will be the one to grab hold of the star?

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:28.080
Tou no choujou de
At the very top of that tower

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:42.450
Shizuka ni tomotta honou ga atsuku mune o kogashite iku
These flames lit in silence fill my chest with a white-hot passion

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:44.700
Unmei no wa
That's just the Wheel of Fortune

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:52.370
Butai no ue de odorasareteiru wake ja nai
It's not like I'm being forced to dance on this stage

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:54.620
Tobitate
Spring forth

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:58.500
Tashika ni ano hi mitanda
I'm sure I saw it that day

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:02.120
Hajiketa hoshi no kirameki
The brilliance of a star that has burst open

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:08.580
Iroaseta yakusoku ni yubi ga fureru made
Until my fingers reach out to touch that faded promise

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:12.660
Makuake mae ni hajimaru
It will start before the curtain rises

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:16.200
Me no mae de tsuzurareteku
And be spelled out before our eyes

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:19.790
Umarekawatta watashi wa
Having been reborn

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:23.620
Koko de kimi ni aeta
I was able to meet you here

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:27.250
Mou ichido
Once again

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:33.770
Seisho Music Academy

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:33.770
Spring Vacation / First Day

00:06:32.290 --> 00:06:35.000
Oui, J'atteris a 15 heures demain.

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:35.080
Yes, I'll arrive in Paris
tomorrow at 3 PM.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.120
See ya, Banana!

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:38.660
Expect a souvenir, okay?

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:40.950
Futaba, hurry up!

00:06:40.950 --> 00:06:43.620
You carry some luggage, too!

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:44.790
Well, then...

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:46.750
We're off!

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:51.580
Starlight Hall

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:58.120
It sure is quiet when everyone leaves.

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:03.250
The only ones left are me and Junna-chan!

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:06.370
Wait, you're going to take pictures of THIS, too?

00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:10.160
The next Seisho Festival is the 100th.
It's a big deal!

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:13.500
These are all important moments
that we need to get on film!

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:17.200
Are you okay... with not going home?

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.250
Huh?

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:23.660
It's just that... I decided that I wouldn't
go home until I graduate.

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:28.580
If you're doing this because
you're worried about me or something...

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:32.160
Junna-chan, you wanna eat udon?

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:36.410
This is where I want to be.

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:41.910
Sure. I'll have some.

00:07:43.130 --> 00:07:44.640
Seisho Music Academy

00:07:43.130 --> 00:07:44.640
New School Year

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.790
Okay, as of today, we're second-year students!

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:52.450
Okay, Junna-chan, give it your all!

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:54.000
Wait!

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:58.580
As an upperclassman, as well as our student council rep,
I have to make sure not to embarrass myself!

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:02.370
It's all the same, but it feels new!

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:08.870
Wow... Those're the new students.

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:11.330
They're all nervous and worried stiff.

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:13.830
This is new to us, too...

00:08:13.830 --> 00:08:16.330
Actor Training
Department

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:18.790
Okay, this is the second-years' classroom.

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:21.370
I look forward to spending the next year together!

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:26.160
Spring vacation is over,
and everyone is raring to go, huh?

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:29.120
Huh?

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:34.370
Naruse and Osaka aren't here yet, are they?

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:37.370
It looks like they dropped out.

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:38.120
What?!

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:39.370
No way!

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:46.860
Sayo Naruse

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:46.910
This is my first duty as a
second-year chairperson, huh?

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:53.080
Right!

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:56.540
We have to move forward, to make it
an even better performance this year.

00:08:58.120 --> 00:08:58.790
Yeah.

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:00.500
100th Seisho Festival

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:00.500
Auditions Commence

00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:03.920
Performance Training Classroom

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:08.870
The 100th Seisho Festival will be
our second performance of "Starlight."

00:09:08.870 --> 00:09:12.080
The auditions for the main cast will finally start today!

00:09:12.370 --> 00:09:14.950
This time for sure I will achieve a flawless victory.

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:17.120
You're going down, dear Tendo Maya!

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:19.370
I'm gonna get the part of Flora!

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:21.580
Then I'll be Claire!

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:24.330
The next lead will obviously be me!

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:25.700
You're heavy...

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:28.370
Daiba-san.

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:30.200
Oof...

00:09:30.450 --> 00:09:33.040
May I have a word with you?

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:34.830
Sure.

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:40.700
We're already on the next auditions, huh?

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:43.200
It still doesn't feel real...

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:49.450
I mean, it's still so clearly burned
into my mind: our "Starlight."

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:55.580
That ultimate stage, just for us,
that we made together...

00:09:56.290 --> 00:10:00.040
I wonder if we can still have it... that same stage.

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:04.410
Even if it's the same cast with the same members,

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:07.040
the same performance will not exist.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.450
That's true, but...

00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:10.620
The girls have made their decision.

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:17.540
There was sure to be despair, suffering,
and rage beyond our comprehension.

00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:22.870
I said that, didn't I? That we should go for the lead roles.

00:10:23.410 --> 00:10:25.830
There are those for whom it will not come to be,
however earnestly they try.

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:30.620
It is an impossible dream, one to which they give their all,
yet there are those that will leave the stage behind.

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:32.660
A favored idol...

00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:34.620
a voice that flourishes wonderfully...

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:37.580
an expansive field of vision over the entire stage...

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:40.290
Even with all that, why won't you-?!

00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:46.370
Hurry up and decide, will you?!

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:49.250
Just wait a little bit longer...

00:10:49.490 --> 00:10:56.120
99th
Seisho Festival

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:54.160
If you're not making a serious effort because
you wish to remain "everyone's Banana"...

00:10:55.160 --> 00:10:56.160
I...

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:01.910
I will not forgive you, Nana Daiba.

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:04.910
Maya...chan.

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:15.910
Nana?

00:11:16.540 --> 00:11:17.830
Junna-chan.

00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:20.080
Oh, are those pictures from our celebration party?

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:21.620
Yeah. Wanna see?

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:23.660
Oh, the chairperson!

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:26.160
Nice shot!

00:11:27.250 --> 00:11:29.540
Wait, you took these too?!

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:35.620
Only two months have passed,
but it's still kinda nostalgic.

00:11:37.540 --> 00:11:42.330
Our "Starlight," here at the Seisho Festival...

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:44.120
I love it.

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:46.200
I love it, too.

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:48.000
Yup! Me, too.

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:55.450
With Group B supporting us backstage,
we in Group A get to sing and perform.

00:11:56.250 --> 00:12:01.200
A stage made just for us,
made by all the members of the 99th class.

00:12:02.330 --> 00:12:06.290
I wonder if we'll never have
the same kind of performance again.

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:13.200
I wonder if I can stand on that stage...

00:12:13.450 --> 00:12:14.120
Huh?

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:16.450
I mean, a stage is a living thing.

00:12:16.700 --> 00:12:20.620
Even if it's the same "Starlight,"
it's impossible to have the exact same stage!

00:12:21.330 --> 00:12:23.870
And there are people who aren't here anymore.

00:12:23.870 --> 00:12:24.370
Yeah!

00:12:24.750 --> 00:12:30.870
That's exactly why we have to practice more and more,
and have a way, way better performance!

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:33.370
Karen-chan?

00:12:33.370 --> 00:12:36.330
Hey! Don't stand on the bench, Aijo!

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:39.410
This is a stage. My stage!

00:12:39.790 --> 00:12:42.080
And I made sure to take off my shoes.

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:44.410
I'm not worried about the shoes!

00:12:45.540 --> 00:12:47.410
You like high places, don't you, Aijo?

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:48.620
Yep! I like 'em!

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:49.950
Places like Tokyo Tower!

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:57.000
Always following the chance that there's a better stage...

00:12:57.870 --> 00:13:00.000
But, to me...

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:05.080
That "Starlight" is the best. It can't be topped.

00:13:12.590 --> 00:13:17.090
Bath

00:13:16.410 --> 00:13:17.120
A giraffe...

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:21.450
How cute.

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:33.290
Huh?

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:36.750
Good evening, Nana Daiba.

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:39.410
Do you find it blinding?

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:40.950
What?

00:13:41.910 --> 00:13:43.160
I understand.

00:13:43.950 --> 00:13:46.410
A real... giraffe?

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:49.660
The Revue.

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:53.660
It is a song and dance woven
into a mesmerizing stage show.

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:58.540
The more "shine" that a Stage Girl feels,

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:05.540
the more freely the lighting equipment, the sound
devices, and the stage mechanisms all begin to move.

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:11.950
The play, the song, the dance,
the shine of the Stage Girl...

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:14.540
This stage responds to it all.

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:16.580
"Shine"?

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:21.410
The one who presents us with
the most dazzling of revues

00:14:21.410 --> 00:14:24.700
shall find the path to becoming
the Top Star opened before her.

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:26.700
"Top Star"?

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:30.450
The one who stands atop the stage of fate.

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:36.160
She makes her talent blossom limitlessly
within the lead role,

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:40.870
a role with a brilliance that
transcends time and lasts for eternity.

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:44.950
I don't care about that. At all.

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:49.000
I understand. However...

00:14:49.870 --> 00:14:54.450
what if you could stand atop any stage you desired?

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:55.450
Any stage?

00:14:56.620 --> 00:15:00.620
You have one as well, do you not? A blinding stage...

00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:04.040
One which you will never experience again,
though you reach for it.

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:07.160
A blinding stage that satisfies the shine.

00:15:07.870 --> 00:15:11.750
Is it blinding? I understand.

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:16.370
Can it really be any stage?

00:15:16.830 --> 00:15:19.000
No matter when, or what kind?

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:23.200
Will you participate in the auditions?

00:15:27.580 --> 00:15:28.870
I understand.

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:42.660
This is... how serious you are?

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:45.950
Did something happen that changed you?

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:48.950
Is it blinding?

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:50.120
What?

00:15:50.700 --> 00:15:52.450
I am blinding.

00:15:54.040 --> 00:15:55.410
What happened to you?

00:15:56.580 --> 00:15:57.790
I can't reach it.

00:15:59.450 --> 00:16:00.250
You'd go this f-

00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:03.700
Position Zero.

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:07.830
It's so blinding that I can't reach it.

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:17.040
Congratulations.

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:20.950
Is it blinding?

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:22.950
Yes, it is.

00:16:23.870 --> 00:16:26.330
The one who has passed this audition...

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:29.040
is you, Nana Daiba-san.

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:35.000
And now that you are the Top Star,
what is the "stage" that you have sought?

00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:40.450
A repeat performance of "Starlight"
at the 99th Seisho Festival.

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:43.200
A shine like a jewel on fire,

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:46.660
blissful days that glitter like a rainbow...

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:48.200
I want that again.

00:16:49.160 --> 00:16:53.200
Even now... that stage is blinding.

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:00.080
Very well.

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:21.580
For you of the 99th class, your program will be...

00:17:22.370 --> 00:17:23.370
"Starlight."

00:17:23.870 --> 00:17:26.200
I love "Starlight"!

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:27.370
Me too!

00:17:27.830 --> 00:17:32.370
Oh, "Lumière des étoiles"? Sounds good.

00:17:32.950 --> 00:17:34.750
"Star... light"?

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:38.910
But, why "Starlight"? And why now?

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:42.040
What's gotten into everyone? Junna-chan?

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:43.080
What?!

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:44.790
Junna-chan?

00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:48.950
W-well, you suddenly called me by my first name...

00:17:49.370 --> 00:17:50.080
Daiba-san.

00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:54.540
Actor Training Department

00:17:53.250 --> 00:17:54.290
Huh?

00:17:56.870 --> 00:17:58.290
First-years headed for the 99th Seisho Festival

00:17:58.290 --> 00:17:59.710
Nana Daiba

00:17:58.290 --> 00:17:59.710
The Stage of Fate

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:05.540
This is how the cycle began.

00:18:06.080 --> 00:18:09.200
A repeat performance of the 99th Seisho Festival...

00:18:10.290 --> 00:18:15.250
Precious friends, a precious stage,
such precious days, all repeated.

00:18:15.790 --> 00:18:18.580
When I'm in those repeat performances,
nothing scares me.

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:22.250
There's no growing up, and no becoming an adult.

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:24.790
The suffering that is forced upon you...

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:30.040
the pain of trying new things,
the sadness of giving up because it hurts too much...

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:32.370
I will protect everyone from all that!

00:18:37.160 --> 00:18:39.000
That's right! Banana!

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:40.000
Huh?

00:18:40.250 --> 00:18:42.950
Nana, you're like everyone's banana!

00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:46.830
Because I'm sweet and kind and nourishing?

00:18:46.830 --> 00:18:49.120
And I can even ease stiff shoulders?

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:51.120
Y-yeah...

00:18:51.120 --> 00:18:52.500
Yeah, yeah!

00:18:53.910 --> 00:18:59.080
I was thinking about how I could make
that same stage again, when...

00:19:04.750 --> 00:19:09.750
I should have been able to reach it,
but it's still too blinding.

00:19:13.620 --> 00:19:15.330
Congratulations.

00:19:17.410 --> 00:19:20.120
The one who has passed this audition...

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:22.910
is you, Nana Daiba-san.

00:19:23.250 --> 00:19:28.620
And now that you are the Top Star,
what is the "stage" that you have sought?

00:19:33.790 --> 00:19:35.620
It's still so blinding.

00:19:38.250 --> 00:19:42.620
I do not know how many times
we have done this, but... Very well.

00:19:43.290 --> 00:19:45.160
Hey... Why?

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:48.870
Why are you doing this for me?

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:53.330
The moment a Stage Girl becomes a Top Star,

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:58.500
the fusion of "wonder" and "shine"
produces a most wondrous reaction...

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:02.370
An eternal sparkle, in a moment of combustion...

00:20:03.040 --> 00:20:06.660
An eternal stage no one can foresee!

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:10.790
I... I wish to see that.

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:15.750
An eternal stage... that no one can foresee.

00:20:26.790 --> 00:20:29.700
For you of the 99th class, your program will be...

00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:32.250
Who... is that?

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:31.910
"Starlight."

00:20:52.330 --> 00:20:53.290
What?

00:20:58.290 --> 00:21:00.450
Are you okay, Karen-chan?

00:21:01.120 --> 00:21:04.620
I just can't stop... thinking about sandwiches...

00:21:08.040 --> 00:21:09.580
K..Karen-chan!

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:12.000
Are you okay, Karen-chan?

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:15.000
She's fine. The girl's a rock!

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:17.080
You're so heartless, Banana-chan!

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:19.790
Hey, you all right, Karen?

00:21:20.540 --> 00:21:24.410
We have a transfer student who'll be joining us
in the Actor Training Department as of today.

00:21:24.410 --> 00:21:27.750
I know it's unexpected,
but please give her a warm welcome.

00:21:27.750 --> 00:21:28.790
Huh?

00:21:31.910 --> 00:21:35.080
This hasn't happened before...

00:21:37.040 --> 00:21:39.580
Who is... that girl?

00:21:38.830 --> 00:21:40.050
Hikari
Kagura

00:21:43.160 --> 00:21:46.410
I danced a whole lot today too, so let me ride the bike!

00:21:46.410 --> 00:21:50.540
We're walking home to build up strength!
The taxi fare is five million.

00:21:50.540 --> 00:21:52.790
If you mean my T-shirts and towels,
I folded them and put them away.

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:53.620
But...

00:22:03.750 --> 00:22:05.660
I wonder what happened.

00:22:06.500 --> 00:22:10.200
Maybe always having the exact same stage is boring.

00:22:12.410 --> 00:22:15.790
A stage of fate, one that no one can foresee...

00:22:16.910 --> 00:22:20.290
And yet, no matter who shows up,
my "repeat performance" won't change.

00:22:21.290 --> 00:22:22.750
Hikari Kagura-chan...

00:22:25.000 --> 00:22:28.750
I want her on my stage, too!

00:23:59.650 --> 00:24:04.450
Next Time
Toward the Light

00:24:00.450 --> 00:24:02.830
Revue Starlight.

00:24:02.830 --> 00:24:04.330
I understand.
